  "title": "Tip-out sheet"
 },
 "description": "Works out how a restaurant shares tips, two ways, as the free tip-out sheet on restaurantdoctorai.com does. method percent: a server's tip-out to support roles, each a percentage of the server's net sales or tips, with the total tip-out, what the server keeps from their tips, and an error-level check when the tip-out is more than the tips. method pool: a tip pool shared by hours, with optional points for each role, rounded to the cent with the rounding remainder placed on the largest share. Takes the figures in any currency; a figure that isn't sent is never counted as 0. Returns the split, how it was worked out, the Department of Labor's published points on tips with their sources, and a link to the free tip-out sheet. It only works out a split from the numbers sent; it doesn't say whether a tip-out or a tip pool is allowed. The figures aren't stored; only an anonymous daily count of calculator runs is kept.",
